    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="0499" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg479"/>

                <head>Mr. Pruyn to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Kanagawa</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 30, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the satisfaction to transmit
                    herewith, No. 1, a convention for the reduction of duties, concluded with the
                    Japanese government. The form has been changed, as it was desired to avoid the
                    necessity of exchange of ratifications, instead of which the ministers are to
                    send me a letter forthwith formally sanctioning the action of their
                    plenipotentiary, of which they have already informally approved.</p>
                <p>Agreements as to future negotiations for bonded warehouse system are yet to be
                    signed; also in reference to Osacca and other incidental points.</p>
                <p>I will send original Japanese and Dutch versions, certified, by way of
                    California, or by first good private opportunity.</p>
                <p>Meanwhile I should be pleased to receive from the Treasury Department any printed
                    rules in its possession for regulation of bonded warehouses.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident in
                            Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d472-a1.xml" xpointer="d472-a1"/>
            </div>
